no-Kubernetes tripwire: armed (kubectl, helm, flux and k3s on PATH record and fail every call; KUBECONFIG unset)
✔ src/broker is its own tree: Node’s standard library and its own files, nothing from core, no package (3.397185ms)
✔ core reaches the broker only through its client, and the client imports the broker’s types only (24.270334ms)
✔ the size budget: no more than 3,000 lines of broker code, tests aside, so one reviewer can read all of it (0.729721ms)
✔ no network surface in the source: no HTTP server, nothing listens on a port, no inspector (2.384964ms)
✔ the fixed protocol: seven verbs, three messages, a fixed refusal list (1.159297ms)
✔ the client has no method that returns a value: no get, resolve, reveal or export (0.249796ms)
